# Local CPU tier configuration.  Copy, then edit:
#
#     cp infra/compose/.env.example infra/compose/.env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. This file is not — so every value here must remain obviously fake.
#
# ── Read this before changing a value ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The placeholders below are deliberately shaped so that a real secret cannot be mistaken for one and
# a placeholder cannot be mistaken for real. Every one starts `CHANGE_ME_`. That is the same
# discipline the AWS side uses: Secrets Manager entries are created with
# `CHANGE_ME_$(openssl rand -hex 16)` and rotated before any real session
# (aws-setup-instructions.md §6).
#
# They are also **at least 32 characters**, which is not cosmetic: the Gateway's `_keys_long_enough`
# validator refuses to start on a shorter key (gateway/app/config.py:103). A placeholder that cannot
# boot teaches the reader to distrust this file, so the padding is load-bearing — keep any
# replacement you write here at 32+ characters even while it stays obviously fake.
#
# **`AUDIT_CHAIN_KEY` is the one you cannot fix later.** The audit trail is a keyed HMAC chain.
# Change this key after any audit event exists and every prior `event_hash` becomes unverifiable —
# there is no migration path and no recovery (rules.md R-31). Locally that costs you a `docker
# compose down -v`; on AWS it costs the evidence. Set it once, at the start.

# ── Secrets (local only — never these values anywhere real) ───────────────────────────────────────

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_local_pg
# HMAC key for the caller-reference pseudonym. The raw client_call_ref never leaves Gateway process
# memory (rules.md R-16); this key is what turns it into the 64-hex `call_ref` that does.
HMAC_KEY=CHANGE_ME_local_hmac_key_pad_0000000000
# Signs the single-use 60-second WSS stream ticket, bound to session_id + sub (D-6).
TICKET_SIGNING_KEY=CHANGE_ME_local_ticket_key_pad_00000000
# See the warning above. Set once. Never rotate against a populated audit table.
AUDIT_CHAIN_KEY=CHANGE_ME_local_chain_key_pad_000000000

# ── Local auth harness ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A no-password JWKS issuer is a TEST HARNESS, not authentication. It must refuse to start outside a
# local profile (rules.md R-05) — the Gateway asserts that, so pointing these at a local issuer while
# DEPLOYMENT_PROFILE is anything but `local-cpu` is a startup failure by design, not a misconfiguration
# to work around.
JWT_ISSUER=https://sih26104.local/auth
JWT_JWKS_URL=http://gateway:8080/local-auth/.well-known/jwks.json
JWT_AUDIENCE=sih26104-gateway
JWT_LEEWAY_SECONDS=30

# ── Operational ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

TENANT_ID=local-demo
MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS=4
SCORER_DEADLINE_MS=800
SCORER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=7
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ── Scorer posture ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave DETECTOR_MODE alone until a real ONNX artifact and a fitted calibration exist. Mock scores
# are transport smoke tests, never evidence of detection, and the mode label travels in every gRPC
# response and audit row so that a mock number cannot be quoted without it (memory.md U-7, U-8).
DETECTOR_MODE=MOCK_SMOKE_MODE_NOT_A_DETECTOR
# One of: research_only | demo_eligible | policy_eligible. Nothing else parses.
# `research_only` is the only honest value until a trained artifact with a fitted calibration and a
# release-manifest entry exists. Promoting this string is a claim about evidence, not a config tweak.
ARTIFACT_STATE=research_only
GRPC_MAX_WORKERS=2
ORT_INTRA_OP_THREADS=2

# ── Provenance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Stamped into the startup banner and into every audit row's parity set. Export it before `up` to get
# a real value:  export GIT_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
GIT_COMMIT=unknown-local
